# OPERATOR STATE. `make pi-ship` does not overwrite the copy on the
# Pi (PI_OWNED in the Makefile). The version in git is only the seed
# for a fresh install, and it will drift from the running one.
# Edit it on the Pi (`sudo pf tui`, House lists, a/d), then apply.
#
# House-segment never-block. Names here (and all their subdomains) are
# removed from the house sinkhole (house_default.domains + hagezi feed +
# house.domains) before the compile. This is the only never-block that
# the house list obeys. The shared never_block.domains keeps registries
# and Google APIs reachable for agents, and here it would protect ad hosts
# under google.com. This is also how to disable a shipped default without
# a change to the repo. A parent frees its children: googleapis.com
# here would free youtubei.googleapis.com. One per line.
doubleclick.net
googleadservices.com
